msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory:3 of
msgid ""
"``variant`` is ``None`` for a format holding a single ``report.pdf``, and"
" the subdirectory's name for a format holding several. ``name`` is what a"
" report prints, and it is the same string the status notes use — "
"``EURIZON-IT24/3``."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.deserialize_pages:1 of
msgid ""
"Pages yielding a deserialize test, by the same rule one stage further "
"down."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.has_integration:1 of
msgid "Whether the whole-document test is collected at all."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.has_integration:3 of
msgid ""
"This is the whole of ``tests.formats.integration``: the metric asks "
"whether a document is checked end to end, and a document with no ``out/``"
" has no expected output to be checked against, so pytest yields nothing "
"for it."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.has_single_page_triple:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether at least one page carries the whole triple — "
"``tests.formats.single_page``."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.has_single_page_triple:3 of
msgid ""
"One such page is the bar, and deliberately so: it means every stage of "
"the pipeline has a fixture somewhere in this document, which is what "
"distinguishes a document somebody tested from a document somebody started"
" testing."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.pdf_extract_pages:1 of
msgid "the blocks fixture, and a document to extract from."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.pdf_extract_pages
