msgid "type"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.pdf_extract_pages:3 of
msgid "Pages yielding a pdf-extract test"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.text_filter_pages:1 of
msgid "the stage's input fixture and its output fixture."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.text_filter_pages:3 of
msgid "Pages yielding a text-filter test"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.DocumentInventory.triple_pages:1 of
msgid ""
"Pages carrying all three fixtures, so that every stage of the pipeline is"
" pinned there."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.InventoryError:3 of
msgid ""
"Raised only when :func:`scan_variant` is asked to be strict, which is "
"what the pytest plugin asks for: a repository pytest cannot collect must "
"fail loudly at collection. The coverage report asks for the opposite and "
"records the problem as a finding, so that a repository with one malformed"
" document can still be measured — a report that refuses to print because "
"one document is broken tells you less than one that prints and names it."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.read_declared_formats:3 of
msgid ""
"A format's name is not a column of ``metadata/formats.csv``: it is "
"composed from three of them, ``AMUNDI`` + ``EN`` + ``24`` making "
"``AMUNDI-EN24``. Composing it again here would be a second implementation"
" of the engine's rule, which is precisely the duplication this module "
"exists to remove one of — and a coverage report that names its documents "
"differently from the suite is a report about a different repository."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.read_declared_formats:9 of
msgid ""
"The engine import this costs was measured rather than assumed: 2 ms, "
"against a walk that reads several hundred file names. It does not take "
"this command out of a commit hook."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.scan_repository:3 of
msgid ""
"``formats`` is the set of format names the repository declares; when it "
"is ``None`` the repository's own ``metadata/formats.csv`` is read, so "
"that a directory under ``tests/formats/`` which the repository does not "
"declare is not counted — pytest would not collect it either."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.scan_variant:3 of
msgid ""
"``strict`` is what the pytest plugin passes: a repository pytest cannot "
"collect must fail at collection rather than be quietly under-collected. "
"The coverage report passes ``False`` and reads "
":attr:`DocumentInventory.problems` instead."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.format_inventory.variant_paths:3 of
msgid ""
"A directory holding a ``report.pdf`` is one document and its variant is "
"``None``. A directory holding subdirectories other than ``pages`` and "
"``out`` is one document per subdirectory. This is the split "
":meth:`FreeportsFormat.collect` makes, and it is made here so that both "
"it and the coverage walk count the same documents."
msgstr ""

